    room_wall_window_title: "The window and the computer",
    faq_a_steps_in_sport: "At the top of Workout Tracking, in a small strip: steps today and this week. The steps will be counted automatically once the app connects to Google Fit / Apple Health in the phone app version – the 🔗 button next to them explains.",
    faq_q_steps_in_sport: "Where is the daily step counter?",
    sport_steps_today_label: "steps today",
    sport_steps_week_label: "this week",
    faq_a_reminders_one_place: "Each reminder comes once, in one place. If the app is open in front of you (on the computer, the iPad or the phone), it shows up there; otherwise it arrives as a notification on the phone only. '✅ Done, thanks!' or 'Got it!' anywhere closes it on every device, and it won't come back. 'Not yet' snoozes it: it comes back every 5 minutes, each time in one place. Ticking the task ✓ in the list also counts as done. To get the notifications on the computer and tablet too, turn on 'Also on computer and tablet' in Settings > Notifications.",
    faq_q_reminders_one_place: "Why does a reminder come only once, and only to my phone?",
    reminder_all_devices_hint: "By default each reminder comes once, in one place: to the phone, or to the device where the app is open in front of you. Done or Got it in one place closes it everywhere.",
    reminder_all_devices_label: "Also on computer and tablet",
    dev_weather_preview_label: "Preview – only on your account:",
    myday_water_info: "8 medium / small glasses of water are about 2 liters on average",
    daily_line_1: "A small step today is still a step.",
    daily_line_10: "On the way to 10 – and today is part of the way.",
    daily_line_11: "A little now beats a lot someday.",
    daily_line_12: "You can start over at any hour, not only on Mondays.",
    daily_line_13: "Five minutes are better than zero minutes.",
    daily_line_14: "Notice one thing that went well today.",
    daily_line_15: "Slowly – but forward.",
    daily_line_16: "Some days the win is just showing up.",
    daily_line_17: "Every ✓ brings us closer to who we want to be.",
    daily_line_18: "No grand plan needed – just the next step.",
    daily_line_19: "Drink some water, take a breath, carry on.",
    daily_line_2: "You don't have to reach 10 today – just keep going toward it.",
    daily_line_20: "What you do on most days matters more than what you do once.",
    daily_line_3: "You don't have to feel ready to start.",
    daily_line_4: "One thing at a time is plenty.",
    daily_line_5: "A quiet day counts too.",
    daily_line_6: "Rest is part of the way.",
    daily_line_7: "Start small – what matters is starting.",
    daily_line_8: "We can pick up right where we left off.",
    daily_line_9: "Talk to yourself the way you'd talk to someone you love.",
    faq_a_daily_line: "A small sentence for the day, in the spirit of \"on the way to 10\". It changes every morning.",
    faq_a_good_things: "In the evening (from 6 PM) a small button shows up under the greeting: write up to 3 good things that happened today – even one is enough. They're saved, and 'Previous days' shows what you wrote before. 'Not tonight' hides it until tomorrow, and you can turn it off completely in Settings > Personalization & Calendar.",
    faq_a_home_countdown: "Mark an event with ⭐ in the calendar (the star next to it in the events list). The nearest starred event in the next 100 days shows under the greeting – '3 days to go · Mom's birthday', 'Tomorrow · …' or 'Today · …'. Tap it to jump to that day in the calendar.",
    faq_a_home_streak: "It counts how many days in a row you had at least one ✓ – anything in My Day, My Routine, My Goals or New Me. It shows up from 2 days on. If today has no ✓ yet, the streak isn't broken – there's still the whole day. And if it ends, it simply disappears quietly, no guilt.",
    faq_a_home_weather: "Turn on 'Weather in the home screen sky' in Settings > Personalization & Calendar and allow location. Clouds, rain, snow, fog or a storm then appear softly in the home screen background, by the weather where you are, updated about every 40 minutes. Your approximate location (rounded to about 1 km) stays only on your device and is checked through our server with MET Norway. It's off by default.",
    faq_a_weekly_note_history: "Yes – press and hold the weekly note (or the small 'Note for the week' pin) on the home screen. Every week that had a note is saved there, with its checklist and text, even if the note was cleared afterwards.",
    faq_q_daily_line: "What's the small sentence under the date?",
