    weekly_note_history_title: "Past weeks",
    weekly_note_history_week: "Week of {date}",
    faq_a_home_focus: "Tap ◎ at the top of the home screen: everything disappears except the one thing for now – what's on at this hour, or the next thing on today's list – with a big ✓, plus Quick Note. After the ✓, the next thing shows up. Tap 'Focus mode ✕' at the top to bring everything back.",
    faq_a_home_planter: "You'll see what's already done today – everything checked in My Day – plus today's water and how many daisies are open. The daisies now count everything you can check in My Day, including routine ✓ and your goals' small steps.",
    faq_a_home_search: "Tap 🔍 at the top of the home screen and type at least 2 letters. Results come from your notes, shopping list, calendar, recipes, notebooks (titles and page text), goals, tables and books, grouped by type – tap one to jump straight there.",
    faq_a_my_day: "My Day brings together what used to be A Peek at Today and My Routine, on one timeline. At the bottom of the home screen you see how much is done, what's now or next (with a quick ✓), a +1 glass of water and New Me. Tap it (or swipe it up) to open the whole day: things with no set time at the top, then everything by the hour – calendar tasks, events and meetings, weekly fixed slots, today's routine, your goals' small steps and New Me meals – with a line for now. Filter by Tasks, Routine or Meetings & events. A ✓ here is the same ✓ everywhere else (My Routine, My Goals, the calendar) and opens a daisy in the corner. 'Edit my routine' opens My Routine (it's also in the menu), and '＋ Add for today' adds a task for today.",
    faq_a_quick_note_hold: "A small menu opens: 'Record a note' (say it out loud and it's written into the note – in browsers that support it), 'To the shopping list' (Quick Note already set to the shopping list) or 'Regular note'. A normal tap still opens a regular Quick Note.",
