    bag_tasks_general: "📝 General tasks",
    faq_a_bag_pockets: "Every notebook, table and task can move to another pocket: open its window (🎨 in a notebook, ✏️ in a table, or tap the task) and pick the pocket. To rename a pocket or change its icon or color, open it and tap ✏️ next to its name. Deleting a pocket deletes everything inside it, so move what you want to keep first. The examples that come with a new bag work the same way – change or delete them anytime.",
    faq_a_my_bag: "My Bag keeps your notebooks, tables and tasks together. Each pocket is a part of life – home, family, work, a trip – with its own name, icon and color. Tap a pocket to open it like a binder: everything in it is on one page, and the colored dividers on the side jump to the other pockets. ＋ adds a notebook, a table (or one built by AI), a task or a new pocket. The filters show only notebooks, tables or tasks, and 🔍 searches everything. The ✅ Tasks card at the top is free for everyone; pockets, notebooks and tables are part of Premium.",
    faq_q_bag_pockets: "How do I move or delete things in My Bag?",
    faq_q_my_bag: "What is My Bag?",
    premium_benefit_bag: "My Bag – pockets with notebooks and tables of your own",
    faq_a_goal_library: "In My Goals, tap ＋ (or a topic, when there are no goals yet) to open the goal library: 12 topics – health, weight, music, learning, money, family and more – each split into areas with ready plans. Every plan shows its stations week by week (or a days challenge, a count or a weight goal) and its daily small step. 'Start this goal' creates it right away, 'Edit first' opens it so you can change anything, and the 'Add to My Routine' switch puts the daily step into your routine at a free hour (tap the hour to pick another) – a ✓ in one place checks the other too. You can also search ('guitar', 'exam'), and '✏️ My own goal' is always there. 2 plans in every topic are free, and the whole library comes with Premium ⭐.",
    faq_q_goal_library: "What is the goal library, and how do I start a goal from a ready plan?",
