    faq_a_food_not_fried_default: "No. Unless it's written (fried, schnitzel, breaded, chips…), food is counted as baked, grilled or cooked in a pan with almost no oil. 'In a pan' means a little oil at most – not frying – and mentioning the oven or a pan doesn't change the portion size. Something fried? Just write it (for example 'fried chicken breast').",
    faq_q_food_not_fried_default: "Does the AI assume food is fried?",
    faq_a_routine_nudge: "When an item hasn't been checked ✓ for more than 3 days (only the days it's due count), a gentle card at the top asks whether it's still part of the routine and whether it works – maybe something should change to move forward:\n• ✓ Yes, keep it – no more questions about it for a week.\n• ✏️ Change – opens the item for editing.\n• 🗑️ Remove – takes it out of the routine.\n• ✕ – not now.\nWhen more than 3 items are waiting (maybe there was a vacation), one card asks about all of them together: continue as usual, or change something – which opens the list of those items, each with ✏️ / 🗑️.\nThe card appears only when ✓ tracking is on and in use. The same item copied to several day tabs counts as one.",
    faq_q_routine_nudge: "Why does My Routine ask me about an item?",
    faq_a_routine_day_tabs: "Yes. In ⚙️ choose 'Days for this tab' – on those days My Routine opens straight on it, and a small dot marks it. A tab named after a day (like 'Sunday') is recognized by itself, and the day templates set the days automatically. When a tab has days, the ✓ question counts only the days its items are due.",
    faq_q_routine_day_tabs: "Can My Routine open on today's tab?",
    faq_a_routine_add_templates: "Tap ➕ in My Routine and choose:\n• ✏️ New empty tab.\n• 📄 Duplicate the current tab – all its hours and items are copied (without the ✓ history). Duplicating a day tab like 'Sunday' suggests the next free day by itself – the fastest way to build a different routine for each day.\n• ⭐ Ready templates (Premium): a tab for each day (Sun–Thu, Mon–Fri, Sun–Fri or the whole week) – empty, or each day as a copy of the current tab – and 10 ready routines with content: calm morning, evening & good sleep, workday, work from home, study day, workout day, balanced eating, calm day, day with kids and weekend. Everything can be edited afterwards.",
    faq_q_routine_add_templates: "How do I duplicate a tab or use a ready template in My Routine?",
    routine_tpl_weekend_items: "09:00 Sleep in + slow breakfast\n11:00 Family or friends\n13:00 Lunch\n15:00 Rest\n17:00 Walk\n19:00 Dinner\n21:00 Movie or a quiet evening",
