    faq_a_workout_calories: "Yes. Every workout gets an estimate of the calories burned – by type, duration and your latest weight (for running and cycling also by speed, when a distance is entered). It shows in the workout list and in the monthly summary (🔥 Burned), and it's added to that day's calorie budget: in the Daily Meal Tracker, in Calorie & Weight Metrics and in New Me's ring. It's an estimate, so it's shown with ~.",
    faq_q_workout_calories: "Do workouts count in my daily calories?",
    faq_a_new_me_flexible_menu: "Yes. ➖ on a meal card removes it from the menu (for example 3 meals, or 2 meals and a snack – at least 2 stay), and '➕ Add back' returns it. The removed meal's calories become free: 🔄 Swap on another meal then offers bigger options, up to your daily plan. The swap window has three tabs: 🍽️ Menu (the program's options), ⭐ Saved meals (your own saved meals that fit the budget) and ✨ Write it – describe what you'd like and the calories and protein are estimated. Every swap can be for today only or from now on.",
    faq_q_new_me_flexible_menu: "Can I change the number of meals in New Me, or eat my own meal?",
