    nm_burned_line: "{n} kcal from workouts – added to today's budget",
    faq_a_calendar_goals_reading: "Yes. Tapping a day in the Monthly Overview also shows, in a separate '🎯 Goals & reading' group, that day's tasks from your goals and books: a days challenge's daily tasks, weigh-in or count reminders, and '📖 Read N pages'. Today's can be ticked right there, like in My Day; other days are for viewing – past days show what was done and how many pages were read, future days show what's planned. To keep the calendar clear, only special days get a small mark: 🎯 on a goal's date and 📖 on the day a book should be finished.",
    faq_q_calendar_goals_reading: "Do goals and reading show up in the Monthly Overview?",
    faq_a_meetings: "Tap ＋ in Calendar View (on Monthly Overview, All Events or Meetings) and choose 🤝 Meeting at the top – next to ✅ Task and 📅 Event, which work as before. A meeting has a start time and, if you like, an end time, who it's with, a place or link (address, Zoom, Meet…) and notes. Meetings appear in the 🤝 Meetings card – a paper diary of the week with a line for each day; the arrows move between weeks and tapping a meeting opens it for editing. A place opens in maps and a call link gets a '🔗 Join' button. Meetings also show in the Monthly Overview and in My Day with their hours, get reminders like any event, and sync to Google Calendar with the end time, place and details. In My Day a meeting also shows who it's with (👤), and a repeating meeting can also run for just 1 month.",
    faq_q_meetings: "How do I add a meeting, and where do I see my meetings?",
