    daily_focus_pick_hint: "Pick one or a few – no need to do everything",
    daily_focus_not_today_toast: "That's okay – we'll ask again tomorrow 🌙",
    daily_focus_not_today_btn: "🌙 Not today",
    login_app_purpose: "NOT10.ai – personal planning and tracking: schedule and tasks, notes, nutrition, fitness, budget and goals, with optional Google Calendar sync.",
    item_updated_success: "Changes saved ✓",
    books_page_ask_hint: "So the progress bar and the daily reading task pick up from the right place.",
    books_page_ask_of: "of {total}",
    books_page_ask_title: "📖 Which page are you on?",
    books_back_to_page_toast: "📖 Back to Reading – from page {n}",
    faq_a_reminder_snooze: "It works like a snooze: another reminder arrives 5 minutes later, and it keeps coming back every 5 minutes until you tap '✅ Done, thanks!' or 'Got it!' (up to 6 times if there's no response). On the phone's notification, ⏰ snoozes and ✅ marks the task done without opening the app; tapping the notification or swiping it away counts as 'Got it!'. Snoozing works even when the app is closed, and if the task is marked done in the meantime, the reminders stop on their own.",
    faq_q_reminder_snooze: "What happens when I tap 'Not yet' on a reminder?",
    reminder_snoozed_toast: "Another reminder in 5 minutes ⏰",
    faq_a_new_me_body: "📏 Measurements: enter waist, hips, arm and thigh in cm (any of them), plus an optional 'Other' measurement with its own name (for example chest). Each measurement gets a card with the latest value, the change since the first measurement and a mini chart; there is one entry per day – saving again on the same date updates it. 📸 Progress photos: add a photo once a week (the same light and pose work best). With two photos or more, a before/after comparison appears – drag on the photo to compare, and tap any photo to choose whether it's 'Before' or 'After', or to delete it. The photos are completely private: they are kept in a private storage area that only this account can reach, they are never shared, and they are deleted together with the account.",
    faq_q_new_me_body: "Where are measurements and progress photos, and who can see the photos?",
    faq_a_new_me_checkin: "Every day from 19:30, a '🌙 How was today?' card appears in New Me's whole day (in the backpack) with three quick questions on a 1–5 scale: hunger, energy and mood. After saving, it shrinks to a small summary that can still be edited. In 📅 Monthly calendar, each day shows its mood emoji, and the 'Check-in vs. the menu' card compares the month's averages on days the menu was kept (3+ meals checked) with the other days – to see whether the menu is filling and gives energy.",
    faq_q_new_me_checkin: "What is the evening check-in?",
    faq_a_new_me_reminders: "In ⏰ Meal reminders, turn on the switch and choose a time for each meal – by default breakfast at 10:00, lunch at 13:00, a snack at 16:00 (it can move to any time between 13:00 and 19:00) and a light dinner at 19:00. You can also choose something at 21:00 – something small to eat (up to ~100 kcal), just a drink, or nothing. Each meal can be turned off separately and its time changed. The reminder arrives as a notification even when the app is closed (notifications need to be allowed on the device – if they aren't, the screen shows a button), it shows what's on the menu, and tapping it opens New Me. No reminder is sent for a meal that is already checked ✓, and a reminder that is more than an hour and a half late is skipped. Each meal keeps its name and time, so dragging the meals only changes the order they're shown in.",
    faq_q_new_me_reminders: "How do meal reminders work?",
    faq_a_new_me_shopping: "Open 🛒 Shopping list in New Me and choose how many days to shop for – 3, 5, 7 or 'Other' (1–14). The list is built from the menu for those days (including today-only swaps, without a planned free meal and without meals already checked today). Identical items are combined into one line with the total quantity (for example 'Eggs – 14'), and everything is grouped: protein, dairy, fruit & veg, bread & grains, pantry. Untick anything already at home and tap 'Add to shopping list' – the items go straight into the app's Shopping List. Lines that are already there with exactly the same wording aren't added twice. Quantities are approximate (dry weight for rice, lentils and pasta).",
    faq_q_new_me_shopping: "How does the shopping list from the menu work?",
    faq_a_new_me_journey: "New Me counts the journey day by day, with no end: 'Day 1' is the day the program started, and the top card shows the next milestone – first week (7), one month (30), two months (60), 90 days and beyond. 'My journey' shows the milestone path, the current and best streak, good days, plus the weight: start, now and goal, how many kg are down, the percentage of the way to the goal and a chart with the goal line (weight added here is the same record as in Periodic Weight Tracking). A good day = ✓ on at least 3 of the 4 meals without going more than 10% over the calorie goal; a planned free meal never breaks the streak. 🏅 Achievements are earned automatically – first meal, full day, streaks, milestones, kg down, goal reached, measurements, photos and more – each with a small celebration, and they can be shared.",
    faq_q_new_me_journey: "What are 'Day X', the streak and the achievements?",
    faq_a_new_me_free_meal: "Once a week (Sunday to Saturday) one meal can be replaced with a free meal of up to about 700 calories. Tap '🍕 Plan a free meal' under today's menu (or choose it from the 🔄 Swap list), then pick the day and which meal it replaces. On that day the meal card turns into a free meal: you can write what's on the plate and the calories (optional – ~700 if left empty), and tap ✓ as usual. The day still counts as a good day in the streak even if it goes over the calorie goal. A planned free meal is left out of the shopping list, and it can be cancelled at any time. It can be planned up to 7 days ahead, also into next week; picking another day in the same week simply moves it.",
    faq_q_new_me_free_meal: "What is the planned free meal?",
    faq_a_new_me_swap: "Tap 🔄 Swap on any meal in today's menu. First come options from the whole menu (both plans) with similar calories – within ±15% of that meal – and below them the rest of the menu. Each option shows the calorie difference compared to now (for example +30). After choosing, decide each time: 'Today only' (tomorrow the regular meal returns) or 'From now on' (it replaces that meal every day). The difference is simply accepted: the day's total at the top of the menu, the ring and what's left for today update by themselves, and a big difference shows a gentle note. A meal swapped for today only has a 'Today only' tag and a '↩ Back to regular' button. To change the order of the meals, drag the ⋮⋮ handle – each meal keeps its name and reminder time, and only the order changes. A meal that was already checked ✓ moves its check to the new choice.",
    faq_q_new_me_swap: "How do swaps and the meal order work in New Me?",
    nm_sales_f7: "A progress journey with milestones, achievements, body measurements and before/after photos",
    nm_sales_f6: "An automatic shopping list from the menu, and meal reminders",
