    faq_a_google_calendar_reconnect: "Usually because Google ended the app's access – for example after some time, after a password change, or if access was removed in your Google account. When that happens, Settings shows a warning that the connection to Google Calendar has expired, with a '🔄 Reconnect' button (and a short message appears when you open the app). Tap it and approve again – everything you added in the meantime is sent to Google within a minute or two, so nothing is lost.",
    faq_q_google_calendar_reconnect: "Why didn't an event I added reach Google Calendar?",
    google_calendar_reconnect_toast: "Google Calendar needs to be reconnected – you can fix it in Settings ⚙️",
    settings_google_calendar_reconnect_btn: "🔄 Reconnect",
    settings_google_calendar_reconnect_warning: "⚠️ The connection to Google Calendar has expired, so new events aren't reaching Google. Reconnect – anything added in the meantime will be sent right after.",
    apptour_m_books_link: "A finish-by date adds a daily reading task to My Day, and finished books can count toward a reading goal in My Goals.",
    apptour_m_books_text: "A cozy reading corner: books to buy, up next, reading and read – with a progress bar, a finish-by date and a shelf of the books you've finished.",
    faq_a_books_deadline: "For a book you're reading, set 'Finish by' in its details (or tap the 📅 chip on its card). The card shows the days left and how many pages a day you need, and My Day gets a daily task like '📖 Read 15 pages' – ticking it adds those pages to the book, and unticking takes them back. The number is set at the start of each day, according to where you are. To count books toward a goal, tap '🎯 Link a reading goal' and choose a 'Count to a target' goal from My Goals – every book you finish adds +1, and moving a book back takes it off. Lowering the page, or tapping 'Finished 🎉' just to try, doesn't make the task disappear: a lower page counts as a correction, not as reading, and a book moved back from ✅ Read to 📖 Reading returns to the page it was on (if that isn't known, the app asks which page you're on).",
    faq_q_books_deadline: "How do the finish-by date, the daily reading task and the reading goal work?",
    faq_a_books_what: "In the menu, under Lists, open '📚 Reading Corner'. There are four tabs: 🛒 To buy, 📚 Up next, 📖 Reading and ✅ Read. Tap '+ Book' and write the name – if the book is found in Open Library, its cover, author and pages fill in with one tap (otherwise it gets a colourful cover). Move a book along with one tap: 'Bought ✓', '▶ Start reading' and 'Finished 🎉'. While reading, update your page (or tap +10 / +25) to see the progress bar and your 🔥 reading streak grow. Finished books stand on a wooden shelf with your ⭐ rating and a line you loved – tap a book to open it again. Not found by name? Typing the author's name shows that author's books – and when Open Library finds little, Google Books is searched too.",
    faq_q_books_what: "How do I keep track of the books I want to buy and read?",
